To install the Steep application:

1. Open the Steep .dmg Disk Image included alongside this document.
2. Drag the Steep icon onto /Applications.
3. If Steep.app exists, click Replace in the dialog.
4. Do not move or rename Steep.app

Note: For security reasons, Steep MUST be installed in /Applications. Steep will refuse to start if installed elsewhere.

To run the Steep application:

1. Open the /Applications folder.
2. Double-click the Steep icon.

If you wish to use the Command-Line Interface:
    An -cli is in the zip along with the .dmg.
    You must first install the app from the .dmg into /Applications and copy the -cli to your /usr/local/bin.
    The -cli will load its libraries dynamically from the app in /Applications.
